# EVERY SET-ALGEBRAIC LAW THIS TREE CLAIMS, WITH ITS VERDICT. One row per (law, subject): which
# law, which relation or instance, whether it holds, and the cardinalities that decide it.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THIS IS THE RELATION examples/soundness.rs IS A VIEW OF, AND IT ANSWERS A QUESTION NEITHER
#    checks/ NOR arithmetic/ ASKS. A check says the DOCUMENT contradicts the model. An arithmetic
#    site says you cannot COMPUTE here. This says the QUERY does not compute what it claims to --
#    a defect in the machinery rather than in the evidence, and the only one of the three that
#    accuses nobody's filing.
#
# ⛔ THE CONTRACT EVERY LAW KEEPS: one plain SELECT, no leading WITH, returning exactly
#   `(law, subject, holds, detail)`, with `holds` NULL only on the roster row that found nothing
#   to check. Same shape as checks/ and arithmetic/, same reason -- a law with an empty subject
#   set must report ⛔ VACUOUS rather than vanish from a GROUP BY.
-- algebra/roster.sqlc joined to each law's own subjects.
:union(ALL algebra/decomposition.sqlc,
           algebra/owed_equality.sqlc,
           algebra/leaves.sqlc,
           algebra/jagged_layers.sqlc,
           algebra/composed_demand.sqlc,
           algebra/integrity.sqlc,
           algebra/carried.sqlc,
           algebra/owed_remainder.sqlc,
           algebra/settled_remainders.sqlc,
           algebra/borne.sqlc,
           algebra/arithmetic_class.sqlc,
           algebra/remainder_standing.sqlc,
           algebra/exposure_standing.sqlc,
           algebra/searches.sqlc,
           algebra/part_regimes.sqlc)
